{
  "requirement": "The SDK MUST allow `Validation::validate` callbacks to run without a configured\nmodel provider. A callback that does not invoke the agent interface MUST NOT\nfail merely because no agent is configured.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has two obligations: `Validation::validate` callbacks MUST be able to run with no configured model provider, and a callback that doesn't use the agent interface MUST NOT fail only because no agent is configured.\n\n**Covered by the marked test.** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[runner_reuses_negative_judgments_and_records_only_callback_observations]` is marked `{test}` for this requirement.\n- It builds `Validator::new(&graph, ...)` and never calls `with_agent`. In `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph/runtime.rs`, `Validator::new` sets `agent: None` and `renderer: None`.\n- It runs `validate_node(&9)` against the `Memory` graph. The `Validation` impl on `Memory` does not call `ask()`, because `ask_in_callback` is false by default.\n- It asserts `.await.unwrap()`, so the call must return `Ok` with no agent configured. It also asserts `result` is false.\n- It checks that the callback ran (`state.started == vec![9]`) and that an evidence record was stored.\n- It then calls `check_node`, a second `validate_node` and a `v2` validator, all still without an agent. They all behave normally.\n\n**Contrast case.** In `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls`, a callback that does call `ask()` with no agent returns `NoAgentConfigured`. That test is marked for other requirements. It shows the test setup can tell the two cases apart, so the `Ok` result above comes from skipping the agent and not from the agent check being absent. The error comes from `Ask::execute` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/procedure.rs`.\n\n**Residual gap.** The no-agent scenario only exercises node 9, whose callback returns a false judgment. The requirement does not distinguish judgment results, so I don't count this as a gap.\n\nI found no unacknowledged gap, and no `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "d91fe10e1f6df32599cf59831ba7351a49c19ea4b6184a47acd609ffe13eeabb",
